{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460837-winter-s-teeth-10-and-crimson-thaw-1-spoilers","id":1460837,"title":"Winter's Teeth #10 and Crimson Thaw #1 *spoilers*","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-22T07:46:07-07:00","id":1460837,"title":"Winter's Teeth #10 and Crimson Thaw #1 *spoilers*","content":"So, WINTER'S TEETH ended yesterday with a bang and much to my surprise, they simultaneously released CRIMSON THAW, which is the start of the next arc. I don't know if there's plans to do any more comics after these but I am pleased with the overarching story arc. If we don't get any more comics after the initial 13 (10 issues for Winter's Teeth and 3 for Crimson Thaw), I have to say that we really got ourselves a solid multimedia property out of this.<br /> <br /> Really, I think WINTER'S TEETH is probably one of the best V5 products to come out as it really manages to capture that classic V:TM feel. I think that's probably because Tim Seeley, in addition to being a veteran horror comic writer (Hack/Slash) is also a World of Darkness gamer himself. Tini Howard and Blake Howard also contributed greatly to the success with the latter having the brilliant idea to add game material to the backs of the book.<br /> <br /> I like Cecily and think she's probably the best vampire character to come out since Lucita, Bell, Jan, and Beckett among the other signature characters. The whole idea of an Anarch who &quot;sold out&quot; and hates herself for it is an idea with legs, especially if you go with the idea she's an early Goth/Rock Girl that finds herself bewildered at how all of her friends have since turned into soccer moms. She might be a bit too old for that and it would have been better to make her a product of the 90s versus the early 80s but I'm not too harsh on this decision.<br /> <br /> I have more than a little amusement, though, from the &quot;ironic Hell&quot; that Cecily was sentenced to by being made Prince of the Twin Cities, though. This is something that is very personal, though, because it is the exact sentence that my most dedicated Anarch was sentenced to when he was turned into the Prince of Gary, Indiana when he called in the very ironic boon he'd gotten from a Justicar. He had that same bewildered expression on his face Cecily did at the end.<br /> <br /> I think what works best about this comic is it makes a careful balance of making sure it's clear that all of the vampires in the city are evil bastards (even Cecily) but they're humanized. Friends, loved ones, and lovers with the occasional act of utterly scummy violence. I also enjoyed Tim's take on the fact the Anarch vs. Camarilla thing is just theater even if I don't agree with it. Anarchs and Cammies are really just using the sects as an excuse to fight for power and reach across the isle whenever its conveinant.<br /> <br /> (Calder Wendt should be grateful that Carfax is a Tremere, though, as he would have been executed for killing the Prince and fudging up the hunter response)<br /> <br /> I will say the Moritician's Army was a disappointment, though, and will go down in history as the dumbest branch of the Second Inquisition we've seen. The whole fact that they chose to attack at night, even if an hour before dawn, shows that they squandered a massive opportunity. A bunch of cocky sonsabitches who got themselves slaughtered for no good reason. I know there's no story if they attack during the day but smart vampires have an escape route and defenses (or ghouls).<br /> <br /> Do I wish this was an ongoing? Yes, very much so. Sadly, I don't know if we'll be getting anything after Crimson Thaw--especially with the writing and art team changeup.<br /> <br /> But I will give them props for the set up: LUPINES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Au